ave  4.1 million cases of coffee 90 where are  140 000 of them are dying due to coffee  19. for the children itself we have  uh between age 0 and 5 we have 121  000 cases or 2.9 percent and  for the age between 5 and 80 we have  four hundred and twenty four thousand so  basically ten point one percent so  around thirteen percent of coveted 19  cases in indonesia are from children  below 18.  so how much does poverty or  living conditions  affect the potential for children to be  harmed by covert 19 even indirectly  well basically it's interesting that our  children who are live in poor area are  living in the  village we have we which have low  literacy or coffee 19 they are more  prone to the infection because of you  know that their parents might not have  access to the  good health care information about  coffee 19 how to treat them as early as  possible so in the rural areas and the  poor area usually the cases of covet 19  from children are higher  and we've seen that according to the  indonesian pediatric society more than a  hundred indonesian children have died  every week since july have died from  covert 19. so why are children seemingly  so  susceptible to infections and deaths  there  yes i think it is interesting because  at the july indonesia face its second  wave uh the cases of the coffee 90s are  soaring high you know that  the hospital occupancy in only two weeks  at the june the hospital occupancy was  around 30 percent and then at the july  it's soaring high  up to 80 percent and the daily death of  coffee 19 cases was around 1 000 and 500  cases at that time we have delta florian  who have really massive spreading and  outplays and become the dominant  dominant mutation in indonesia and of  course with that rapid spread the number  of the  victims including from the children are  increasing rapidly however in the health  care facilities  usually hospitals in indonesia are more  prepared to fight with  adult or elderly cases of coffee 19 and  man