ous only  when they have the full-blown symptoms  of the disease  that helped authorities get sars under  control  through strict quarantines  when it comes to mers  we know even less about transmission  than we do with sars because even fewer  people have contracted it which means  even fewer opportunities for study but  but it's believed that people can catch  it directly from animals and and camels  are a prime culprit a human to human  spread is also possible through close  contact but  as far as i can tell  no one has yet identified the exact  mechanisms of that spread

